---
import Post from '../../layouts/Post.astro';

export const meta = {
  title: 'Why me?',
  date: '2024-11-06',
  description: 'Why not hiring me is a mistake.',
  kind: 'essay',
} as const;
---

<Post meta={meta}>
  <p>
    Disclaimer: this is not the technical side of me.
    If you want to get to that directly, take a look at my resume <a href="/resume.pdf">here</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>1. I am foolish.</h2>

  <p>I am foolish enough to believe I can do something without knowing a single thing about it. I just begin. I have realized that not knowing how complicated things can get actually works to my advantage. I discovered this about myself when I built a minimal version of React back in 2019, when I was just starting to code.</p>

  <h2>2. I am hungry.</h2>

  <p>I have an insatiable hunger for knowledge. In pursuit of it, I recently came up with a rule for the small choices I make throughout the day. For any activity I come across (apart from the necessary routine), I ask myself two questions:</p>

  <ul>
    <li>Will I learn anything new?</li>
    <li>Will I have fun? (Having fun helps.)</li>
  </ul>

  <p>The best choice is one that leads to both. For me, that's reading, solving problems, and writing.</p>

  <h2>3. I am jealous.</h2>

  <p>I am jealous of everyone around me who I think is better than me. The competitive person in me wants to be the best person I know, and the hardworking person in me pushes me to be just that. I may not be smart enough to find the most efficient way, but I brute-force my way to where I need to be. And as we know, slow as it might be, brute force works!</p>
</Post>
